-- Gina Hinojosa / same-sex-marriage  (chair 2 -> 1, CHAIR_MOVED_HELD_SET_CLEARED)
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning = 'Chair moved from 2 to 1 on 2026-10-08 (migration 1906). Migration 1903 held this row out rather than repair it, because a citation repair may not move a chair and this member''s own record proves a rung the chair did not hold. The operator cleared the held set on 2026-10-08. THE RECORD: she is a coauthor of HB 188 (86R), "Relating to the prohibition of housing discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation or gender identity or expression". ⚖ THE RUNG: Season 2 rung 1 is the ONLY rung that adds anti-discrimination protection to equal marriage -- "full legal equality: equal marriage plus protection from discrimination (such as in jobs and housing)". Rung 2 is marriage equality alone. This row already sat at rung 2, so the marriage half was granted; her own bill supplies the half that distinguishes rung 1, and in the example the rung itself gives. ⚠ Her later filings -- the repeal of the offense of homosexual conduct (88R HB 2055, 89R HB 1738) -- span rungs 1 to 3 and so do not conflict with rung 1 under the latest-filing rule; a band that CONTAINS the rung is not a disagreement with it.', sources = ARRAY['https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=86R&Bill=HB188', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=88R&Bill=HB2055', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=89R&Bill=HB1738', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gina_Hinojosa']::text[], updated_at = now()
